ce mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality"],"id":"long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.62 (Perturbed-family maximality and the three-branch recurrence)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.62, p. 61, label thm:perturbed-family-maximality","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Use the family and adjacent pair of Definition 6.61, and assume in addition that $B<g$. At capacity $C'=4C+g$, the largest admissible updated value is $t(x_+)$ if $4o+p_+\\le g$, and $t(x_-)$ otherwise. After this choice, apply the take-if-possible rule to an additional weight $W=2g+4$. The resulting remainder is\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\n g-4o-p_+,&4o+p_+\\le g,\\\\\n 4r+g-p_-,&4o+p_+>g\\ \\text{and}\\ 4r+g-p_-<W,\\\\\n 4r-g-p_--4,&4o+p_+>g\\ \\text{and}\\ 4r+g-p_-\\ge W.\n \\end{cases}\n$$*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.above_newSum_le_capacity_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.thm-perturbed-family-maximality%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.PerturbedFamily.AdjacentCut.above_newSum_le_capacity_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d